Naming (no clashes with POSIX / libc)
-------------------------------------
Everything that behaves differently from its POSIX namesake carries the ue_ prefix.

  functions       ue_read(), ue_open(), ue_write() ...
                  raw syscall wrappers: they return -errno and never set errno
  struct tags     struct ue_stat, struct ue_timespec ... (raw kernel layouts)
  typedefs        ue_sigset_t, ue_fd_set, ue_cpu_set_t, ue_siginfo_t,
                  ue_stack_t, ue_timer_t, ue_idtype_t, ue_kernel_fsid_t
  struct fields   ue_sa_handler, ue_sched_priority,
                  ue_st_atime, ue_st_mtime, ue_st_ctime
                  (glibc defines these names as macros)

Left as is, because they match POSIX: macros and constants (O_RDONLY, SYS_*, ...),
raw_syscall*, and plain scalar typedefs (ssize_t, off_t, pid_t, ...).
Including a libc header that defines the same macro with the same value only
gives a "redefined" warning.


